/* "blocked" cells: a plain, fully opaque fill — no gradient, no transparency,
 * no image resource. Two different hatch approaches were tried here (a tight
 * repeating-gradient, then a data-URI SVG background) and each broke on a
 * different real print backend that never showed up in any preview: a data
 * URI can paint before its async decode finishes, and gradients using the
 * CSS "transparent" keyword have a long-standing Firefox print bug where the
 * transparent stops rasterize as opaque black instead of see-through. A solid color has
 * no load step and no alpha to mishandle, so it can't fail either way,
 * regardless of which engine ends up rendering the printed page. */
